schema: test/v2
epic: E-DFLOW
wu: E-DFLOW.W5
level: working-unit
tests:
  unit:
    files: ["ui/src/components/*.test.tsx (24 suites, one per component)"]
    asserts: "each component against ITS OWN contract, not generic rendering: every state in its @states line renders and is distinguishable, every documented keyboard path fires, and the @avoid boundaries representable in code hold. Each W4 finding this WU fixes carries its own case so a regression reds - StatusPill 200->ok / 404,500->warn / 301,101,unknown->muted / null->'…' with the reason phrase reaching title+aria-label; CopyButton's labelled AND D2b icon forms, the confirm flash and its timeout, and the icon form's 24px hit floor (the 22px borrow both W4 runs made is the bug this pins); Notice's positive-outcome state; Button's in-flight state; CutMarker's real-vs-apparent truncation (humanBytes rounded both sides to one string, so a genuine cut announced itself as no cut); Select's type-to-filter and arrow/Enter selection; StatusLine's precedence - an authoritative positive beats a stale error"
    count: 222
  integration:
    files: ["ui/src/components/collection.test.tsx"]
    asserts: "the collection's bounded contract, the part no per-component test reaches: (1) the barrel exports exactly the 24 T1/T2 roster names - a set equality, so a component that skips the barrel reds - and each mounts standalone with no screen around it; (2) every @madeof edge composes rather than re-draws - StatusPill and StatusLine each render exactly one TonedText, KeyValueRow and FormRenderer render CopyText's copy affordance, Button/CopyButton/IconButton are three un-nested <button> elements over one shared shell, JsonRenderer falls back through TextRenderer, Notice's action slot takes a Button; (3) all 29 @avoid redirects resolve to a real export that the roster also mounts. This is the WU's requirement in one file: the collection is a vocabulary, not a folder"
    count: 62
  e2e: { waived: "flow e2e is W7 per the epic plan - same wording as W4. No screen consumes the collection yet (Q2), so there is no user-visible flow to drive; FlowList/FlowDetail/BodyViewer keep their inline copies deliberately" }
gate0: "green - cargo fmt --check + clippy -D warnings + cargo test --workspace green across every crate; the WU adds no Rust logic beyond xtask ui specimens and verify-doc's specimen check, both covered by xtask/tests"
ui: "npx tsc -b clean - it caught five wrong prop names the jsdom mount test had accepted silently, which is the process note the result report keeps: a mount-only assertion proves less than it looks like, and the typecheck is what makes it bite. npx vitest run 439 passed across 38 files"
render: "cargo xtask ui specimens --check drives headless Chrome over file:// with no flags - the way a reader double-clicks - asserting a clean console (thrown, rejected AND console.error/warn) and every specimen mount non-empty across all migrated design docs. DEC-16's single mermaid diagram verified the same way: 1 svg, 9 nodes, no leftover pre.mermaid, data-mermaid-src kept for the diff layer"
